{
  "name": "Driver COD Briefing",
  "description": "Daily 9pm Edmonton evening wrap-up: triggers the RxDeliver driverCodBriefing function, which pushes every driver who worked today a day summary AND delivers the owner wrap-up via in-app message + push. The agent relays nothing on WhatsApp and only reports failures.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 21 * * *",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "driver_cod_briefing",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.2.0"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "run_and_report": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "It is 9pm — the evening driver COD wrap-up briefing is running now. Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. Run this bash command (it triggers the RxDeliver briefing function):\ncurl -s --max-time 300 -X POST 'https://base44.app/api/apps/68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6/functions/driverCodBriefing' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BASE44_SERVICE_TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n\n2. Check the returned JSON. The function itself ALREADY delivers everything: each driver who worked today gets a push + in-app message with their summary, and the app owner gets the full wrap-up via in-app message + push notification. DO NOT compose or send any WhatsApp briefing to the owner — the owner asked for in-app + push only (Oct 13 2026).\n\n3. If success is false, or the function errored/timed out, retry once via the call_base44_backend_function tool (app_id 68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6, function_name driverCodBriefing, payload {}). If it still fails, notify the owner with a SHORT WhatsApp note saying the briefing failed and why. If any driver in the pushes array shows 0 sent with errors, include a one-line note about that too.\n\n4. If everything succeeded, end silently — no WhatsApp message, no briefing content relayed.",
            "x-base44": {
              "description": "Evening COD wrap-up: pushes handled entirely by the function",
              "title": "Driver COD evening wrap-up"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
